  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Logo Integrity**\n\nOkay, I\'ve confirmed the initial `img/logo.png` retrieval and reviewed the image dimensions. The curl output shows a PNG of 1689 x 336. Now, I\'m focusing on validating its visual integrity and considering the need for an SVG alternative or fallback mechanism. I\'m checking if the image loads correctly and displays as expected.\n\n\n**Confirming Logo Details**\n\nI\'ve got confirmation on the logo\'s authenticity; it\'s the high-res white logo with the red isotype for dark backgrounds, with 8-bit RGBA and non-interlaced. I verified the image locations; it\'s correctly placed in `/img/logo.png` and `/public/img/logo.png`.  Relative and root paths work in the HTML. Now, I\'m setting up `/style.css` with Google Fonts (Inter and Inter Tight), custom CSS variables for colors, and base styles. I\'ve defined font families and am tweaking the scrollbar and selection styles to match the brand.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Flair**\n\nI\'m now creating a dynamic red gradient animation using a keyframes rule and a corresponding class that applies a linear gradient, text clipping, and infinite animation. I\'m also building the background with geometric shapes, using a container to manage the positions of five elements, including circles, a diamond, a hexagon, and a triangle, each styled with gradients and clip-paths.\n\n\n**Crafting Animated Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details of animating the background elements. I\'m focusing on morphing clip-paths and applying transforms with smooth transitions on the various shapes. I\'ve defined default shapes and specific states, including the hero section\'s configuration with specific sizes, positions, and opacities for the circle elements, building the foundation for dynamic visual effects.\n\n\n**Refining Shape Transformations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the transformations applied to the animated background shapes. I\'ve defined initial configurations for the hero section, including positions, sizes, opacities, and clip-paths for circles, diamonds, hexagons, and triangles. I\'m tweaking scale and rotation values for the shapes, with specific configs for \"Nosotros\" section. I\'m exploring variations in opacity and scaling for each shape.\n\n\n**Adjusting Shape Parameters**\n\nI\'m now deep in the configuration for Servicos and Cobertura sections with complex transformations for shapes. I\'m fine-tuning rotations, scales, positions and opacities. I\'m also optimizing clip-path definitions and adjusting each element to match its respective states, ensuring dynamic behavior for each section\'s visual aesthetic, and I\'m currently focused on the Servicios\' section.\n\n\n**Configuring Visual Sections**\n\nI\'m now implementing distinct visual configurations for the Servicos, Cobertura, and Flota sections. For the \"Servicios\" and \"Cobertura\" sections, I\'ve applied significant rotations, large scales, and reduced opacities. For \"Flota,\" the focus shifts to small scales and very subtle opacities. I\'m building on this foundation for the Stats, Contacto, and Footer sections, keeping the opacity faded.\n\n\n**Finalizing Interactive Effects**\n\nI\'m now implementing interactive effects for specific shapes, focusing on hover states and scroll-triggered animations. I\'m setting opacity and scale configurations for individual shapes and adjusting radar ring animations with keyframes to create a pulsating effect. I\'m adding scroll reveal animation with fade-in and slide-up transitions for various sections of the layout.\n\n\n**Adding Visual Overlays**\n\nI\'m now integrating crucial visual layers. I\'m focusing on a noise overlay using SVG turbulence for a subtle effect, and implementing a section transition flash for visual emphasis. I\'ve configured custom cursors with dot and ring elements. I am also working on the scroll progress line for added interactivity.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 27
      nanos: 512496118
    }
