  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing JavaScript Implementation**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the `/script.js` file. I\'m starting by reviewing the JavaScript interactions and required logic. My initial focus is on the preloader, specifically its duration, the counter\'s increment from 0 to 100 with letter spacing adjustments, and the horizontal\n\n\n**Observing Section Interactions**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the section observer implementation, particularly how it interacts with the geometric shapes. The script determines viewport entry via `IntersectionObserver` and applies updates to the `bgLayer`\'s `data-section` attribute, along with triggering a flash effect. I am considering edge cases.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategies**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the implementation strategies. For the parallax effect with geometric shapes, I\'m considering several options: wrapping each shape, using an inner div or a parallax wrapper, or leveraging CSS custom properties (`--parallax-y`) for seamless section transitions without transform collisions. This seems promising. I\'m also planning the Navigation: a fixed top bar and a mobile menu with a hamburger toggle that reveals a fullscreen overlay and locks body scroll, triggered by scrolling past 60px. Finally, I will implement scroll reveal using `IntersectionObserver`, and animated counters with the same logic.\n\n\n**Implementing New Features**\n\nI\'ve just added several enhancements: a scroll progress bar, a custom desktop cursor with hover effects, and a magnetic button interaction. The progress bar accurately reflects scroll position, while the custom cursor adds visual flair. Finally, the magnetic effect on the main buttons reacts to cursor movement, adding a subtle, dynamic element to the UI.\n\n\n"
