  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Markup Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `/index.html` file\'s markup, carefully checking off each requirement from the prompt. I\'ve confirmed the `DOCTYPE` and meta tags, paying close attention to the `lang=\"es\"` attribute and the meta tags for character set, viewport, and SEO, including the title \"CONEXPET | Transportamos el futuro\" and meta description.\n\n\n**Adding Open Graph Details**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the Open Graph protocol now, and I\'ve plugged in the necessary tags for the `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:type` and `og:image`. Next, I\'ll link the favicon to either `img/isotipo.png` or `img/logo.png`. I\'m also now moving to the CDN/Stylesheet details.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the visual elements, starting with a centered, fading-in logo and a growing red progress bar, which will be 1px high, along with a number counter. The overall duration is targeted at approximately 2.4 seconds, followed by a fade-out and staggered hero reveal. Then I\'ll focus on the fixed geometric background shapes and the section flash overlay. I will also incorporate the custom cursor and noise overlay. Finally, I will address the navigation bar, making it fixed at the top.\n\n\n**Constructing Navigation Elements**\n\nI\'m now creating the navigation bar. I\'m centering links to \"Nosotros,\" \"Servicios,\" \"Cobertura,\" \"Flota,\" and \"Contacto.\" A red \"Cotizar\" button is being added to the right, using a pill shape and a magnetic effect. For mobile, there will be a hamburger button that toggles to an \"X,\" leading to a fullscreen overlay menu with large, bold, centered links.\n\n**Developing Hero Section**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the hero section. It will be 100vh with a centered layout. It will include a red uppercase eyebrow badge with a typewriter effect reading \"Confiabilidad en cada kil\303\263metro\". A giant H1 follows, saying \"Transportamos el futuro\" with a red gradient. There is a subtitle in a light grey color, describing the services, and a badge with the real operating hours will be added next.\n\n\n**Adding Sectional Information**\n\nI\'m now implementing the buttons and scroll indicator for the hero section. There\'s a green pulse dot indicator with \"Operaciones 24/7\" in an inline flex container. Then, there\'s a red pill button to request a quote and a ghost button to explore services. A red animated vertical line with \"Scroll\" beneath it is also being added for navigation. After that I have began working on the \"Nosotros\" section.\n\n\n**Designing Sectional Content**\n\nI\'m now building out content for the \"Nosotros\" section, incorporating impactful statistics such as \"15+ a\303\261os de trayectoria\", \"500+ clientes corporativos\", and \"98% entregas a tiempo\". I\'ve begun section 3, labeled \"Servicios\", which has a 2x2 grid layout and I\'m currently working on the card details for \"Transporte de Carga Pesada\" and \"Log\303\255stica Integral & Fluidos Vacuum\", including their icons, tags, subtitles, and detailed descriptions, as well as their micro-interactions.\n\n\n**Detailing Sectional Content**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Rutas & Izaje\" and \"Cobertura Nacional & Talleres\" service cards within the grid, giving careful attention to their SVG icons, red pill tags, subtitles, and detailed descriptions. I\'m focusing on the technical analysis and safety standards for the former, and preventative maintenance for the latter. Now I\'m working on the next section: the \"Cobertura\" section, and incorporating the 2-column grid. I\'m focused on the visual elements for the left column, including the animated concentric rings, the radar sweep, and the stylized Ecuadorian map with interactive points.\n\n\n**Mapping Coverage Extensively**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Cobertura\" section, specifically focusing on the geographic scope: Costa, Sierra, Amazon\303\255a, and the road interconnectivity. Four main routes are being added with vertical red lines, connecting Quito, Esmeraldas, Baeza, and a transversal line. I\'m moving on to building out the details for the \"Flota\" section.\n\n\n**Adding Fleet and Contact Details**\n\nI\'m now implementing the \"Flota\" section\'s details, emphasizing key stats: monthly kilometers, active units, coverage in provinces, and companies served. Next, I\'ll move on to the \"Contacto\" section, which uses a 2-column grid. I\'m focusing on the left column\'s details like the eyebrow, heading, paragraph, and contact information with red SVG icons. The right column will feature a quotation form with fields for personal and service details.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
