  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Design Needs**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the user\'s explicit requests. I understand they want a complete redesign, incorporating all existing sections from the current page. The key is an organized, clean, and modern aesthetic. I\'m prioritizing clarity and incorporating their specific adjectives to guide the new design direction.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Direction**\n\nI\'ve established the initial light mode design as clean and modern, inspired by Swiss/Nordic editorial aesthetics. The focus is now on powerful typography and a striking contrast with the red accent. Crucially, a seamless dark mode toggle will be integrated with localStorage for persistent preference. I\'m aiming for an Awwwards-worthy design as requested, incorporating all key elements from the original site map. The header, particularly, will emphasize extreme power and impact.\n\n\n**Crafting User Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the user interface components. I am planning an interactive hero section with a dynamic visual switcher to showcase different service areas. The navigation will feature a clear CONEXPET logo with optimized light/dark mode variations and intuitive links: Servicios, Flota, La Empresa, Cobertura, Intranet, and Contacto. A dark/light mode toggle with smooth transitions is essential, alongside action buttons \"Cotizar Operaci\303\263n\" and \"Acceso Intranet\".\n\n\n**Detailing Service Specifications**\n\nI am now focusing on detailed technical information. I\'m building an interactive service section, complete with drawers or modals to display specifications, fluid types, equipment, and frequently asked questions for each offering. Next, I\'ll flesh out an interactive fleet browser, highlighting the vehicle categories with specs accessible through hover or click interactions. The specs will encompass key elements like horsepower, towing capacity, axles, and GPS tracking.\n\n\n**Mapping Coverage Expansion**\n\nNow, I\'m analyzing geographic coverage and operational reach. I am incorporating over 15 years of industry leadership in hydrocarbons and mining. Specifically, I\'m focusing on the central operating base in Lago Agrio, expanding to Quito offices and operations throughout the 24 provinces. I am planning an interactive national coverage map with estimated transit times. This will cover interprovincial logistics for Amazonian, Sierra, and Coastal regions, and will reflect the Intranet\'s categorizations.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 869676967
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
