    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Logo Colors**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the original CONEXPET logo\'s color scheme. The primary version features dark text and a red icon, optimized for light backgrounds. I\'ve also noted the dark mode adaptation, which involves a brightness and inversion filter to make it fit for use in dark mode!\n\n\n**Defining Default Mode**\n\nMy focus has shifted to establishing the default, light mode. I\'m aiming for a clean, Swiss-inspired aesthetic, using a white background with subtle warm undertones and high-contrast typography in deep graphite. The logo will display its original colors. I plan to incorporate fiery red accents, and razor-sharp contrast throughout!\n\n\n**Refining Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m now refining the dark mode. I\'ve chosen an Obsidian-like background with `#09090B` and `#0D0D11` shades, accented by glowing red `#EF4444`. Card surfaces will be sleek with `#121217`, and I\'m deciding whether to filter the logo or switch it outright. The theme preference will be saved in `localStorage`, with \'light\' as the default.\n\n\n**Detailing Homepage Elements**\n\nI\'m now detailing the homepage elements. I\'m focusing on incorporating a micro-interaction for a phone number link, a secondary line for operational details and a direct link to emergency dispatch. I also want to include a live metrics ticker bar showing key data points: Years of operation, provinces covered, tonnage capacity, and on-time delivery percentages.\n\n\n**Describing Service Details**\n\nI\'m currently focused on detailing the services offered. Each will have an interactive \"View Technical Sheet\" button, opening a modal with specs, equipment details, response times, and a direct form. I\'m also planning a vehicle fleet section with interactive filters, allowing users to sort by category, such as all, 6x4 trucks, vacuum tankers, telescopic cranes, and lowboy & flatbed trailers.\n\n\n**Expanding Company Profile**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Company & Governance\" section. I\'m writing about our history, tracing our origins in Lago Agrio and our growth to serve the oil, mining, and infrastructure sectors. The mission, vision, and core values (HSE First, Operational Excellence, Transparency, Community & Environmental Respect) are next. I\'m then including all our official certifications: ISO 9001, 14001, 45001, the Zero Accidents policy, and BASC/HSE certification, with a client and ally section following. Finally, I\'ll incorporate a logistics radar and national coverage map of Ecuador.\n\n\n**Structuring Internal Portals**\n\nI\'m now structuring the internal portals, covering HR with safety reporting, competency evaluations, and occupational health monitoring. Operational aspects will encompass the JD Edwards ERP, Hesk support, and the SYSFIN portal for suppliers. There\'s also a confidential ethics line. I\'m building an interactive live quote system with origin/destination selection and load categorization.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 890517860
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
