    started_at {
      seconds: 1788611418
      nanos: 451908053
    }
  }
  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Initial Requirements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the initial requirements, specifically the light mode default. The user\'s intent is clear: we are starting with a bright, light background, explicitly mentioning a preference for a clean white or light gray. This architectural foundation, as I see it, is the basis of our whole design.\n\n\n**Defining Color Mode Behavior**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the behavior of the color modes. My focus is on ensuring a seamless, instantaneous toggle between light and dark modes. Dark mode gets an obsidian background with dark, translucent card surfaces, contrasting text, and a vibrant red glow. Light mode, on the other hand, is crisp and clean, with a white background, subtle grey borders, deep graphite headlines, body text, and accents in dynamic red. The logo\'s appearance is also being considered; native colors in light mode, and a contrasting effect in dark. I\'m prioritizing extreme impact in the header.\n\n\n**Crafting Hero Section**\n\nNow, I\'m constructing the hero section. I\'m focusing on an animated subtitle switcher with focus on \"TRANSPORTE DE FLUIDOS VACUUM\", \"MOVILIZACI\303\223N DE RIGs & TALADROS\", \"IZAJE CON GR\303\232AS DE 120 TN\", and \"LOG\303\215STICA PESADA MULTIMODAL\". The sub-headline will project authority. Dual action buttons with a \"Solicitar Cotizaci\303\263n\" primary and a 24/7 support line will be included. A real-time response indicator reinforces this. Finally, an interactive matrix showcasing the four operational divisions is next.\n\n\n**Developing Key Metrics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on quantifiable metrics. I\'m prioritizing a high-impact bar. This includes highlighting key figures like \"+15 Years\" of leadership, \"24 Provinces\" covered, \"120 Ton\" certified lifting capacity, \"99.8%\" operational compliance, and \"0%\" HSE incident tolerance.\n\n**Incorporating Site Content**\n\nI\'m now incorporating the content from the old site and the sitemap. This involves the \"La Empresa & Gobernanza\" section, including the company history, purpose, core pillars, and triple certification (ISO 9001, 14001, 45001). This content helps provide vital context to my plan.\n\n\n**Detailing Service Sections**\n\nI\'m now detailing each service section, focusing on \"Transporte de Fluidos (Vacuum)\" and \"Carga Pesada & Extrapesada (RIGs y Maquinaria)\". For \"Transporte de Fluidos\", I\'m highlighting the 200 bbl capacity, various fluids handled, and ATEX-certified equipment. Interactive technical specs and a \"Ver Ficha T\303\251cnica\" button will be included. \"Carga Pesada\" will showcase the mobility of drilling RIGs, along with the equipment involved. I\'m prioritizing the detailed specs within an interactive experience, and showcasing the management of oversized permits.\n\n\n**Elaborating Industrial Services**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Izaje y Montaje Industrial\" and \"Talleres Especializados y Mantenimiento Propio\" sections. For industrial lifting, I\'m highlighting crane capabilities from 30 to 120 tons (Grove, Liebherr, Tadano), complex maneuvers like oil substructure assembly, and critical rigging plans with 3D simulation. I\'m also focusing on the maintenance base in Lago Agrio, computerized maintenance, original certified spare parts, and 24/7 mobile units. Finally, I\'m working on an interactive vehicle fleet catalog with filters and technical sheets.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive elements, specifically dynamic live filters for the equipment catalog, which will filter between all, 6x4 trucks, vacuum tankers, telescopic cranes, and lowboys/platforms. Each piece of equipment will feature a name, model, a collapsible technical sheet with specs like useful capacity, traction, engine, satellite tracking, calibration certificates, and an operational availability badge. I\'m also planning an interactive map of Ecuador, outlining five strategic hubs (Lago Agrio, Quito, Guayaquil, Cuenca, and Manta/Esmeraldas) and key transportation corridors.\n\n\n**Structuring Intranet Content**\n\nI\'m now structuring the content for the Intranet and corporate portals, adhering closely to the sitemap. I\'m prioritizing a sophisticated, high-fidelity corporate dashboard. The focus is now on the \"Recursos Humanos\" tab, including incident reporting, performance evaluations, employee requests, and medical surveys. I\'m also planning the \"Operaciones & Sistemas\" tab, with an integration with the existing JD Edwards ERP. I\'m focusing on user-friendly navigation and intuitive information architecture for each section.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Intranet Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the additional intranet functionalities. This encompasses the *Mesa de Ayuda Hesk* for IT support tickets, *SYSFIN* for vendor payment inquiries and electronic invoicing, and a dedicated Ethics/Whistleblower channel with a confidential reporting mechanism.\n\nI\'m also working on an intelligent, live quote tool that will let users select origin and destination within Ecuador, specify service types, estimate weight or volume, and see real-time tariff calculations and mileage estimates. This will integrate seamlessly with WhatsApp for direct dispatcher communication. Furthermore, an ethics section, with information about the company\'s commitment to integrity, will be available, along with a comprehensive FAQ section addressing critical operational inquiries. Finally, I\'ll incorporate a contact form.\n\n\n**Validating Quote Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating real-time quote validation, including contact details and base information, such as operational base and office addresses, along with real phone numbers, and an email address for operations, and a direct WhatsApp link.\n\nI\'m considering the corporate footer details; RUC, links to policies, terms, sitemap, and design credits. I\'ve begun to explore CSS variables and Tailwind integration, working on defining the core variables for light mode in `index.html`. These will include background, text, borders, and accent colors to ensure consistent theming.\n\n\n**Implementing Theme Preferences**\n\nI\'m now implementing the theme preferences and leveraging local storage for persistence. I\'m focusing on ensuring users can switch between light and dark modes easily, with the selected mode staying consistent across sessions. My work involves checking local storage, applying the appropriate data attribute, and dynamically updating the toggle button\'s icon. I\'m prioritizing accessibility and a seamless user experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 820182996
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
