  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Light Mode Design**\n\nI\'m now focusing on structuring the CSS for a light mode default. My plan is a bright white background, subtle light tints for secondary sections, and borders in a light gray. I believe the data-theme attribute, or its absence, will control the theme switch. I am thinking that this will be the basis for later themes.\n\n\n**Defining Dark Mode Scheme**\n\nI\'ve specified the dark mode\'s color palette. I\'m going with a pure obsidian background with secondary shades and borders of light transparency on a dark background. The text will be bright white with subtle grayscale variations. The glowing red theme from light mode is present, also. To toggle between themes, there will be a modern toggle button, using SVG sun/moon icons, and saving user preference to local storage to prevent FOUC (flash of unstyled content). Finally, it will be a sleek preloader, that matches the preferred mode.\n\n\n**Analyzing Homepage Structure**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the homepage structure, specifically for the described company. I plan to feature a strong headline and subtext, immediately followed by dual CTAs and floating technical cards. I envision a dynamic stats bar with animated counters.  \"La Empresa & Gobernanza\" will include the company\'s story, values, and certifications. I need to showcase their specialized services as key pillars, and have identified the first division as \"Transporte de Fluidos\".\n\n\n**Detailing Service Divisions**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of service divisions. I\'ve broken them into Vacuum services, Heavy & Extra-Heavy Cargo, Industrial Lifting & Assembly, and Own Workshops & Maintenance. Each service will boast an interactive \"View Technical Sheet\" button, opening a modal with detailed technical specs and safety checklists. I\'m also planning a detailed vehicle fleet catalog with live filters.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 461779306
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
