  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Javascript Core**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `script.js` file. First on the agenda is the light/dark mode switcher, grabbing the theme preference from local storage or defaulting to \'light\'. I\'m designing the logic for icon updates across both desktop and mobile views, and crafting a smooth toggle handler for a seamless user experience. The preloader is also going to be integrated shortly.\n\n\n**Adding Dynamic Effects**\n\nI\'ve got the fast numeric counter near completion, targeting a ~1.8-second reveal with a smooth animation. Next up is the sticky navigation bar, which I\'m designing to dynamically blur and update scroll progress, with classes adapted for both light and dark modes. I\'m also preparing for the hero section with a matrix and typewriter effect, cycling through key service descriptions. I will focus next on the interactive fleet filter and service modals.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Tools**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive tools. Specifically, I\'m working on a route calculator that provides estimated road distance, transit time, and heavy vehicle recommendations when a user clicks on different cities. Simultaneously, I\'m developing a live freight quote calculator. Users will input origin/destination cities and cargo details to get distance, equipment recommendations, and transit time. It will also generate a WhatsApp quote URL and offer an on-page form submission option.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 23
      nanos: 191679075
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
