  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Initial Animations**\n\nI\'ve discovered the initial animation setup! The `.reveal` class uses `opacity: 0;` and `translateY(30px);`. JavaScript, specifically in `script.js`, employs IntersectionObserver to trigger the `.reveal.active` class, which then sets `opacity: 1;` and `translateY(0);`. This is how the reveal animation works. Next, I\'ll see what happens when the project is downloaded.\n\n\n**Analyzing Local File Paths**\n\nI\'ve just realized a critical issue when opening the project locally. The leading slashes in the HTML\'s `<link>` and `<script>` tags, referencing `/style.css` and `/script.js`, cause browsers to attempt loading these files from the root directory. This results in numerous errors, as crucial JavaScript components like the preloader, IntersectionObserver, and all interactive features fail to initialize. This, in turn, breaks the entire page\'s functionality and styling. I need to consider an alternate setup.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 378657246
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
