    thinking: "**Clarifying CSS Integration**\n\nI\'m revisiting the `index.html` file to definitively establish how CSS is being handled. I need to be certain whether we\'re utilizing the Tailwind CSS CDN or if `/src/index.css` is also imported via build tools such as Vite. I\'m focusing on the import statement to confirm.\n\n\n**Analyzing Offline Tailwind**\n\nI\'m now investigating the user\'s reported issue: effects not showing after downloading. My focus is on the offline experience. Double-clicking `index.html` after downloading is the key test. I\'m considering compiling the full Tailwind bundle into a local CSS file. This will ensure functionality even without internet, addressing the user\'s reported problem. I\'m determining the best way to handle the local compilation for a robust standalone HTML template.\n\n\n**Diagnosing Download Failures**\n\nI\'ve reproduced the reported issue by downloading the HTML and opening it locally. The browser, correctly, can\'t find the linked `style.css` and `script.js` files, leading to a cascade of failures. Specifically, the missing CSS makes all custom variables undefined and disables key styling components such as the dark/light theme, background shapes, modal styles, and custom cursors. The missing Javascript prevents the preloader from hiding and hides all elements with the `.reveal` class. The HTML is not self-contained.\n\n\n"
